From d4d2f9330ddac0f53d54fe882c328791e20ad5d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:59:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a pooled card that parks with unpushed state
 stays on its worker

Review of #1247 at 118b512 (comment 6471 on t_01a1ce6551c811ef):

- Park pins unpushed state. kanban_continue, kanban_schedule and kanban_block
  (with the time and dependency parks it routes to) now check the card's trees
  before their write txn (kanban_park_pin.plan). A pool:worker card whose run
  parks here with a dirty tree or commits on no remote is set to
  runs_on [machine:<this worker>] in the same txn, with a pool_pinned event
  (unpushed_state, trees). A later park with every tree clean and pushed (or
  gone) puts it back on the pool (pool_unpinned). Only the gateway that holds
  the run plans the pin (claim_lock has this host's prefix).
- The card's trees are found where they live: the workspace and its children,
  linked worktrees under ~/code/_wt etc. whose worktree-owner marker names the
  card, and trees the park text names.
- A move to self is refused as pool_keeps_pushed only when a tree of the card
  was found and it is clean and pushed; with none found, host_reason stands.
- Drop the unrelated plugin_hooks.json fingerprint churn.
- Test: a no-pin create on a worker gateway with worker_queue set gets
  pool:worker; a placement pin to the ship host and an explicit runs_on stay.
